# Missing hardware/system services in the private container. QML errors always fail.
WARN quickshell.service.upower: Could not connect to DBus\. UPower service will not work\.
WARN quickshell.bluetooth: Could not connect to DBus\. Bluetooth integration is not available\.
WARN quickshell.network.networkmanager: Could not connect to DBus\. NetworkManager backend will not work\.
ERROR quickshell.network: Network will not work\. Could not find an available backend\.
ERROR quickshell.service.pipewire.loop: Failed to connect pipewire context\. Errno: 112
WARN quickshell.service.polkit.listener: failed to create subject for listener: No session for pid [0-9]+
WARN quickshell.service.polkit: failed to register listener on path "/org/omarchy/PolkitAgent"
# The probe uses Sway's layer-shell support, with no Hyprland session.
WARN: \$HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE is unset\. Cannot connect to hyprland\.
WARN quickshell\.hyprland\.ipc: Error making request: QLocalSocket::ServerNotFoundError
WARN: The active compositor does not support hyprland_global_shortcuts_v1\.
WARN: GlobalShortcut will not work\.
# The guest has no power-profiles-daemon (Windows manages power), nor a system bus here.
WARN quickshell\.service\.powerprofiles: Could not connect to DBus\. PowerProfiles services will not work\.
# The canary home has no applied theme; Omarchy's installer writes it on a real disk.
WARN scene: QML FileView at .*/ImagePicker\.qml\[[0-9:]+\]: Read of /home/canary/\.local/state/omarchy/current/theme\.name failed: File does not exist\.
# Omarchy's quickshell build notes plugin folders whose names are not QML module
# names. Real Omarchy 4.5 prints the same; the plugins still load.
WARN quickshell\.qmlscanner: Module path contains invalid characters for a module name: +"/plugins/[a-z/-]+"
